# Generated by scripts/emu/walk-script.py from
#   target/walk-usb-meteor/walk.uart.bin
# Every request waits for the answer to the one before it, and every
# request is written 64 bytes at a time 2 ms apart, so the
# whole walk is a function of guest time and no write outruns the
# 128-byte RX FIFO. Do not hand-edit: re-run the capture and
# regenerate.
# Firmware: the reference image at d6cfaa205, DEFAULT features (esp32c6,server,radio) — no spike_uart0_link, so these are the bytes silicon's own merged-default.bin carries.
# Project: examples/meteor as it stood at d6cfaa205, which is what the spike report §11.2's ledger was measured on. The catalog reorganisation has since moved it to catalog/patterns/meteor with an effect/ subdirectory, so the paths differ and the figures would not compare; git archive d6cfaa205 examples/meteor is how the capture got its copy.
# Link: the USB-Serial-JTAG socket (WALK_LINK=usb), which is the link silicon's §11.3/§11.2 captures went over.

